(2124190,1,''),
(2124190,2,''),
(2124191,0,'Discover a new branch Wired - Wired Variables!'),
(2124191,1,'How do Wired Variables work?'),
(2124191,2,'Variables are used to store values and read them at a later point with Wired. For example, they can be used to store the amount of health points for a user. Variables can belong to users, furni, or even the entire room! You can share them across multiple rooms too. But how do you use them?\n\nWired Variables work different from all existing Wired boxes, because they are not stacked on top of the usual Wired boxes, like Triggers and Effect. Instead, Wired Variables form a new kind of Wired stack (lets call it a \"Variable stack\"), one that defines how the Variable works.\n\nIn a usual Wired stack, a Wired Effect is stacked on a Wired Trigger. In a Variable stack, there is one \"WIRED Variable\" and additionally you can add Variable Add-Ons on top of the stack to bring further configurations to the Wired Variable. The boxes that go on a Variable stack all share a similar design, so it\'s easy to know if a box belongs on a Variable!'),
(2124191,3,''),
(2124192,0,'The Wired boxes on this page is a combination of the types of Wired you all know and love, like Triggers, Effects and Conditions. The ones on this page are used specifically to work with Wired Variables'),
(2124192,1,''),
(2124192,2,''),
(2124193,0,'Variables are used to store values and read them at a later point with Wired. Variables can belong to users, furni, or even the entire room! You can share them across multiple rooms too.'),
